# Digest of the extracted RC netlist behind the SIGNED post-layout row of record
# (`verify_postlayout_rc`).  The netlist itself is a ~5 000-card extractor output and is not
# committed (rule: never commit rawfiles); this file is the `raw` its provenance block hashes,
# the pattern `spicexplorer_harness.hashes.recompute` documents for an untracked rawfile.
#
# Produced by the verifier's OWN run: layout/gen_ldo.py -> layout/signoff.py
#   --stages guards,build,cd,drc,lvs,pex --pex-mode RC   (kpex 2.5D, stitch_mesh on)
# on the GDS this verifier rebuilt, DRC 0 / LVS matched.  The extractor stamps its own run date
# into the file, so a re-extraction gives a DIFFERENT digest for the SAME layout -- what is
# reproducible is the mesh census and the scorecard, both recorded here.
#
# mesh: 3096 nodes, 3101 zero-ohm edges contracted,
#       3101 cards collapsed, n_zero_r_cards = 0,
#       220/243 device pins on the mesh, open nets 0,
#       15/15 named ports anchored on a kpex [Pin] node.
# cards: 5461 Rext + 21 rhigh primitives = 5482 R, 186 C; zero-valued Rext cards: 0
#       (so postlayout.floor_zero_r() floored nothing -- it is a no-op on this netlist).
#
